{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q3xcJyKnGJE2ELinhmHLh8","type":"tool_result","content":"src/gen-template-manifest.test.ts\nsrc/gen-template-manifest.ts\nsrc/index.ts\nsrc/registry-types.ts\nsrc/repo.ts\nsrc/template-registry.ts\n\nsrc:\n__testutils__\n_shared\nbasics\ndev\nevents\ngaming\ngen-template-manifest.test.ts\ngen-template-manifest.ts\nharness\nindex.ts\nregistry-types.ts\nrepo.ts\nsocial\nsports\ntemplate-registry.ts\n\nsrc/__testutils__:\nrender.ts\n\nsrc/_shared:\nlayout.ts\ntext.ts\nwhy.test.ts\nwhy.ts\n\nsrc/_shared:\nlayout.ts\ntext.ts\nwhy.test.ts\nwhy.ts\n\nsrc/basics:\nhello-world\nindex.ts\nregistry.ts\n\nsrc/dev:\napp-store-screenshot-frame\nbench-delta\nindex.ts\nog-card\nregistry.ts\n\nsrc/events:\nbird-walk-sightings\nhomebrew-serving-card\nindex.ts\nregistry.ts\ntalk-timer\n\nsrc/gaming:\ncrossword-grid-card\nindex.ts\nregistry.ts\nspeedrun-pb-recap\n\nsrc/harness:\nagent-timeline\nindex.ts\nregistry.ts\n\nsrc/social:\nepisode-audiogram\nindex.ts\nregistry.ts\ntestimonial-proof-card\n\nsrc/sports:\nindex.ts\nlap-telemetry-card\npowerlifting-meet-recap\nregistry.ts\nswim-time-drop-card\n{\n  \"$comment\": \"The daily run. Edited by humans only — the agent never touches pipeline/. Times are wall-clock caps per agent call; a phase is re-called until it marks itself done in journal/<date>/state.json or runs out of calls.\",\n  \"agent\": \"claude\",\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"remote\": \"origin\",\n  \"dayTimeoutMin\": 270,\n  \"variantsMax\": 3,\n  \"limits\": {\n    \"$comment\": \"The account's session limit, as the agent CLI reports it (Claude Code streams the five-hour and seven-day windows on every call; Codex reports nothing, so a Codex day runs as before). A call the limit rejects does not count against the phase: the runner keeps the tree as journal/<date>/limited/tree.patch, waits for the window - never longer than waitMaxMin, which a five-hour window always fits and a seven-day one never does - and calls again, at most waitsPerDay times. waitAt: before a call, a five-hour window at or past this is waited out first, so the call is not cut halfway. sevenDayStopAt: preflight refuses the day when the seven-day window is past this, since a cut day could not wait for it. graceSec is added to every wait (the CLI's clock is not this machine's). Waits do not count against dayTimeoutMin, so the scheduler's own cap (ExecutionTimeLimit in schedule/one-a-day.task.xml) has to cover dayTimeoutMin + waitMaxMin.\",\n    \"waitAt\": 0.9,\n    \"waitMaxMin\": 300,\n    \"waitsPerDay\": 2,\n    \"graceSec\": 90,\n    \"sevenDayStopAt\": 0.95\n  },\n  \"phases\": [\n    { \"id\": \"scout\",    \"prompt\": \"10-scout.md\",    \"output\": \"10-scout.md\",    \"timeoutMin\": 20, \"maxCalls\": 2 },\n    { \"id\": \"plan\",     \"prompt\": \"20-plan.md\",     \"output\": \"20-brief.md\",    \"timeoutMin\": 15, \"maxCalls\": 2 },\n    { \"id\": \"build\",    \"prompt\": \"30-build.md\",    \"output\": \"30-build.md\",    \"timeoutMin\": 45, \"maxCalls\": 3, \"revisePrompt\": \"35-revise.md\" },\n    { \"id\": \"critique\", \"prompt\": \"40-critique.md\", \"output\": \"40-critique.md\", \"timeoutMin\": 15, \"maxCalls\": 2, \"revisePrompt\": \"45-recritique.md\" },\n    { \"id\": \"ship\",     \"prompt\": \"50-ship.md\",     \"output\": \"50-ship.md\",     \"timeoutMin\": 30, \"maxCalls\": 2, \"onlyIf\": \"decision=ship\" }\n  ],\n  \"revise\": {\n    \"$comment\": \"The critic's NO SHIP is a review, not the end of the day (lib/revise.mjs). When the critic rejects work that exists - critique done, decision no-ship, at least one variant - the verdict moves aside as journal/<date>/40-critique.r<n>.md, build is called again with phases[].revisePrompt appended (answer the verdict, in the same id and folder, rendered into the next variant letter), and the critic judges again with its own revisePrompt. At most maxRounds rounds a run; 0 turns it off and the first verdict stands, as it did until day 013 (2026-10-02), which was closed 22 minutes into a 270-minute day with the fix named in the critique. Rounds live inside dayTimeoutMin; each build call still has its own cap and budget. A day that ends rejected keeps its tree as journal/<date>/rejected/tree.patch, and `node pipeline/run.mjs --date <date> --from revise` takes it up again (at least one round, same roster slot unless --roster or --model says otherwise).\",\n    \"maxRounds\": 2\n  },\n  \"packs\": {\n    \"$comment\": \"Preferred pack vocabulary. The plan phase picks an existing pack when one fits; a new pack needs one sentence of justification and at most one new pack lands per day.\",\n    \"vocabulary\": [\"social\", \"dev\", \"music\", \"education\", \"business\", \"science\", \"news\", \"personal\", \"ops\", \"community\", \"sports\", \"events\", \"health\", \"finance\"]\n  },\n  \"roster\": {\n    \"$comment\": \"Who runs today when the runner is called with --agent random (the scheduler is). One slot is drawn per day, weighted; the runner walks the draw order and takes the first CLI that is installed and logged in, so an agent that is not on this machine costs a log line, not the day. --roster <id> pins one slot by hand. avoidRepeat \\\"hard\\\" ranks yesterday agent behind every other one, so with two agents installed the CLI alternates and the weights choose WHICH slot of it runs; \\\"soft\\\" only damps the repeat (repeatPenalty) so the draw stays genuinely random; false forgets yesterday. entries[].adapter is merged over adapters.<agent> for that slot only. The spread is deliberate: the journal is more interesting when the same brief is attempted by a heavyweight one day and a cheap model the next, and a no-ship day from a small model is a real result, not a failure.\",\n    \"avoidRepeat\": \"hard\",\n    \"repeatPenalty\": { \"agent\": 0.3, \"slot\": 0.1 },\n    \"$models\": \"claude: aliases fable|opus|sonnet (+[1m] for the 1M-context variant) and haiku. codex: model slugs 