{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffNQu7BBFMngRspZDoQs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rj14Qjw7QKZNVtq5ZzPsGC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF' 2>/dev/null || node -e \"\nconst fs=require('fs');const f='src/community/qsl-card/v1/qsl-card.ts';let s=fs.readFileSync(f,'utf8');\nconst rep=(a,b)=>{if(!s.includes(a))throw new Error('missing '+a);s=s.replace(a,b)};\nrep('\\\"who\\\": \\\"Amateur radio operators confirming contacts with paper or e-mailed QSL cards, gathered around their loggers (World Radio League, Wavelog, Log4OM), eQSL/LoTW/QRZ and POTA/SOTA activator circles\\\"',\n '\\\"who\\\": \\\"Ham radio operators who owe every station they worked a QSL card, gathered around their loggers (World Radio League, Wavelog, Log4OM) and POTA activators.\\\"');\nrep(JSON.stringify(['QSL cards for ham radio contacts, one card per QSO, rendered from the ADIF log record (call, date, UTC, band/MHz, mode, RST, grid)'],null,2).replace(/\\n/g,'\\n  '),\n JSON.stringify([\n 'On the World Radio League forum, the \\\"QSL Card Generator\\\" thread opens (57 likes) asking to \\\"select a template ... the appropriate information (other callsign/band/frequency/mode/time/report/etc.) would be auto populated ... a PNG or JPEG could be saved off\\\". A new licensee replies: \\\"struggling with putting together a card\\\".',\n 'It is a batch job: \\\"Auto QSL Card\\\" asks for a card \\\"to all contacts made that day ... if I\\\\'m on a camping trip for 8 days\\\", and page 2 posts a Pillow script drawing text at hand-picked (x, y) points. Wavelog, DigiQSL and S53ZO\\\\'s label tool take ADIF in, but none renders an image per QSO from a command line.'\n ],null,2).replace(/\\n/g,'\\n  '));\nrep(JSON.stringify(['Ham Radio QSL Card: describe the ONE concept this template teaches, in one line, for the Templates page.'],null,2).replace(/\\n/g,'\\n  '),\n JSON.stringify([\n 'One card per QSO from one ADIF record. The props are the ADIF fields in camelCase, in ADIF formats (qsoDate \\\"20261003\\\", timeOn \\\"1432\\\", freq \\\"14.074\\\"), printed the QSL way: 03 OCT 2026, 14:32. BAND is not a prop: it is derived from FREQ with the ADIF 3.1.6 band table, so the two never disagree.',\n 'The decision that matters: a callsign is never ellipsized. The call is sized from its own text, the QSO table reflows 6x1, 3x2 or 2x3 by aspect before any type shrinks, and copy that cannot fit above the floor is refused with an error naming the prop. No photo background in v1: paper, one accent and type.'\n ],null,2).replace(/\\n/g,'\\n  '));\nrep('\\\"command\\\": \\\"m0saic make @one-a-day/community/qsl-card/v1 --template-repo . -w 1280 -h 720 -o out.png\\\",\\n    \\\"try\\\": []',\n '\\\"command\\\": \\\"m0saic make @one-a-day/community/qsl-card/v1 --template-repo . -w 1650 -h 1050 --props @qso.json -o qsl-W1AW.png\\\",\\n    \\\"try\\\": ' + JSON.stringify([\n 'qso.json is one ADIF record: {\\\"call\\\":\\\"DL1ABC\\\",\\\"qsoDate\\\":\\\"20261003\\\",\\\"timeOn\\\":\\\"0915\\\",\\\"freq\\\":\\\"7.074\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"FT8\\\",\\\"rstSent\\\":\\\"-08\\\"}',\n 'freq \\\"432.100\\\" prints BAND 70cm; freq \\\"27.185\\\" (CB) is refused: it is in no amateur band',\n 'myPotaRef \\\"\\\" and myGridsquare \\\"\\\": the lines and their GRID / POTA prefixes go, the rest re-centres',\n '-w 1080 -h 1080 or -h 1920: the QSO table reflows to 3x2 or 2x3; accentColor \\\"#1f5fa8\\\" for a blue card'\n ],null,4).replace(/\\n}/,'\\n  }').replace(/\\n\\]$/,'\\n    ]'));\nrep('\\\"costBasis\\\": \\\"reported\\\"\\n  }\\n};','\\\"costBasis\\\": \\\"reported\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"caveats\\\": ' + JSON.stringify([\n 'No photo background in v1: the card is paper, one accent colour and type. Shack and park photos, the usual QSL face, are a later version.',\n 'One QSO per card. It reads no .adi file: your script maps each ADIF record to the props and calls m0saic make once per QSO.',\n 'RST_RCVD, QSL_VIA and the rig are not printed. BAND is always derived from FREQ, so a log whose BAND disagrees with its FREQ shows the FREQ band.'\n ],null,4).replace(/\\n\\]$/,'\\n  ]') + '\\n};');\nfs.writeFileSync(f,s);\"\nsed -n '/^const WHY/,/^};/p' src/community/qsl-card/v1/qsl-card.ts | grep -v '^        ' | head -60","description":"Fill WHY spec copy in the template"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2016,"cache_read_input_tokens":134972,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2016},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f8f713f-5f69-426b-a3e4-d17888853a78","uuid":"c3bf66bc-a1e4-4ec1-9f04-0641ae982ebe","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:19:02.187Z","request_id":"req_011CffNQtiMh84MAHbCfEsCD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Rj14Qjw7QKZNVtq5ZzPsGC":{"command":"cd /c/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day && python3 - <<'EOF' 2>/dev/null || node -e \"\nconst fs=require('fs');const f='src/community/qsl-card/v1/qsl-card.ts';let s=fs.readFileSync(f,'utf8');\nconst rep=(a,b)=>{if(!s.includes(a))throw new Error('missing '+a);s=s.replace(a,b)};\nrep('\\\"who\\\": \\\"Amateur radio operators confirming contacts with paper or e-mailed QSL cards, gathered around their loggers (World Radio League, Wavelog, Log4OM), eQSL/LoTW/QRZ and POTA/SOTA activator circles\\\"',\n '\\\"who\\\": \\\"Ham radio operators who owe every station they worked a QSL card, gathered around their loggers (World Radio League, Wavelog, Log4OM) and POTA activators.\\\"');\nrep(JSON.stringify(['QSL cards for ham radio contacts, one card per QSO, rendered from the ADIF log record (call, date, UTC, band/MHz, mode, RST, grid)'],null,2).replace(/\\n/g,'\\n  '),\n JSON.stringify([\n 'On the World Radio League for