{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffPPv3aJYdrGqJWoDAPn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I built two of the three variants and left variant c (the ruled-form table) in place. The build gate is clean (layout contract, why-tutorial check and fingerprints), all 280 tests in `npm test` pass, and every render exited 0 with nothing degraded. `state.json` now has `build: \"done\"`, `variants: [\"a\",\"c\"]` and `inPlace: \"c\"`.\n\n**What the template does:** `@one-a-day/community/qsl-card/v1` renders one ham radio QSL card from one log record.\n- **Props:** they are the ADIF fields in camelCase: `stationCallsign`, `call`, `qsoDate`, `timeOn`, `freq`, `mode`, `rstSent`, `myGridsquare`, `qth`, `myPotaRef`, `qslMsg`.\n- **Formatting:** `20261003` prints as `03 OCT 2026` and `1432` as `14:32`.\n- **BAND:** it is worked out from `freq`. I checked the band table against the ADIF 3.1.6 spec page during the build. A frequency outside every amateur band, like `27.185`, is refused with an error that names the prop.\n- **Fitting:** the QSO table rearranges by shape: one row of six in landscape, 3x2 in square, 2x3 in portrait. A callsign is never cut off with \"...\". Copy that can't fit above the minimum readable size is refused instead. The callsign always stays at least twice the size of the table values.\n\n**Variants:**\n- **a (open table with accent rules):** clean. I opened the landscape, portrait and square stills and every string and minus sign is correct.\n- **c (ruled form):** the same layout, but every table cell is boxed in thin ink rules with its label in the corner. It looks most like a pre-printed QSL, so it's the one in place.\n- **b (station panel):** not built. I skipped it to stay inside the 45-minute cap, and `30-build.md` says so.\n\nI also opened the stills for the brief's worst case (callsigns `VP2V/G4ABC` and `VP2V/G4ABC/P`, a 32-character QTH, `143205`, `1296.200`) at five canvas sizes, down to 480x270. Nothing clips. The tutorial's problem and solution pages read correctly.\n\n**Weak spots, written into `30-build.md`:**\n- In c, the accent colour no longer marks a rule under the labels; it is only on the top bar and the TO RADIO tag. That's a small departure from the brief's palette.\n- In c, the horizontal form rules stick out about a pixel past the right edge of the form at some sizes.\n- In c, the form's bottom rule and the footer rule just below it read as a double line.\n\nThe journal is in `journal/2026-10-03/30-build.md`; the per-variant stills are in `journal/2026-10-03/variants/{a,c}/stills/`, and the extra stress renders are in `journal/2026-10-03/scratch/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2966,"cache_read_input_tokens":215286,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2966},"output_tokens":790,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f8f713f-5f69-426b-a3e4-d17888853a78","uuid":"73d2b16f-229c-4b52-a6e3-6bc52110d2ba","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:31:49.936Z","request_id":"req_011CffPPtGfB9CuQTvtqxqAm"}
